e 6  bruno mentioned that he studied kamala's  brother's dna to kind of check if he had  powers as well in which he didn't but he  discovered that kamala's genes were  different and that they had some type of  mutation yes he literally name-dropped  mutation and then as he said mutation  the theme song from the x-men animated  series played  in your genes  like  like a mutation  [Music]  and to top it all off in the credits we  can actually see it is officially  confirmed it literally credits the x-men  97 theme also marvel.com confirms this  which we'll talk about in just a bit but  first let's talk about a key plot point  of the mutants and the x-men being in  the mcu now which is they probably are  not going to get along with society and  society is probably going to view them  as a threat which is a pretty common  storyline for the x-men this is severely  hinted at after bruno tells kamala that  her genes have some sort of a mutation  where kamala then replies with whatever  it is it's just gonna be another label  this implies that a label is indeed  going to be coming with the mutants and  that typically isn't good there's always  been a big number of the human  population specifically governments that  typically hate mutants in fact we have  several storylines that come from this  fact and it seems like the mcu is going  to be no different just another label  implies that mutants will be labeled and  it doesn't sound like that's going to be  a good label people look up to  superheroes in the mcu but now we have  groups like the dodc who are seemingly  hunting down enhanced individuals and  even shooting at enhanced individuals  that they know are kids so we're already  kind of seeing enhanced individuals  being viewed as threats this is probably  going to be amplified when the mutants  make their way into the mcu which they  already have now but when we start to  see more and see some really powerful  mutants some that can you know walk  through walls or read 