ive producer bishop k ali like i  mentioned before and she exclaims oh my  gosh it was the best day of my life when  she got this news however she revealed  that this wasn't always the plan from  the beginning of the show she said i  feel so excited as a viewer of my show  the bishop teen fan girl in me is like i  can't believe it and she continues to  say and the fact that it's kamala it's  her it's like her wildest dream already  came true over the show gaining powers  but then we just gave her one more bit  of the dream it's incredible i'm  overjoyed and as far as the decision to  make her a mutant goes she says that she  didn't find out until she received the  final draft of the final episode she  says they sent me and only me the draft  of the final episode and i immediately  freaked out i emailed kevin feige in all  caps and was like are you doing this  like for real are you sure i'm so  honored i was like yelling at him  through an email i was freaking out this  is the biggest deal in the world and the  fact that it's happening in our show is  crazy so this wasn't actually the plan  the entire time however it could have  been kevin feige's plan the whole time  but not the writers for miss marvel but  it does actually answer kind of a plot  hole for miss marvel and give us a  little bit about the origin of the  mutants she says it wasn't from the  beginning of the show with marvel  something's always a moving piece and  we're trying to solve this question of  if any of kamala's family put on the  bengal would they have powers the answer  was always no from a character  perspective no and the reason for that  was so it could fit into the logic of  the wider mcu so it seems like kamala  has a active x gene that allows her to  use the powers of the bengal this is why  her brother can't use the bangle her  mother can't use it and presumably her  grandmother can't use it either so it's  not because she's a clandestine that  allows her to use the energy and power  o